    "done_when": "Deliver §1 of docs/plans/lane-and-model-routing.html exactly as that section states. The plan is the authority; read §1 and the locked decisions lane-identity (dialect-names), bare-model (imply-when-unique) and derived-names-retire (when-undeclared) before writing. The design report with the call-site census is at ~/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/lane-and-model-design/report.md, and it is the reuse map.\n\n1. The platform schema in reckon/_flight_schema.py accepts a top-level lanes: key. Each lane carries today's backend-block keys plus default_model and a models mapping keyed by model key (for example models.opus). Each model carries model, effort, alias, optional rates with as_of, an optional budget_group defaulting to the lane's, and an optional time_budget override.\n2. Resolution in reckon/flight.py expands each lane into today's backends: entries, so callers reading config[\"backends\"] are untouched. A lane expands to an entry named after the lane (its default model) and to a derived entry named lane-dash-key (for example claude-opus for models.opus) for every model whose derived name matches a legacy backend name. Each expanded entry carries lane, model_key and derived_from. Override layers, including --set lanes.claude.models.opus.effort=xhigh, merge before expansion.\n3. tests/test_flight_lanes.py covers a lane expanding to its default-named entry and its derived legacy entries with lane, model_key and derived_from, and a --set on a lane model reaching the expanded entry.\n4. No value moves: the resolved flight of every project in ~/.config/reckon/mounts.json is byte-identical before and after the change, because nothing declares lanes: yet. Record the comparison in a log under the run directory.\n5. Negative control: applying the override layer after expansion instead of before makes the --set test fail.\n\nGate: tests/test_flight_lanes.py and every tests/test_flight*.py file. Run them with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 in the FOREGROUND, with one log each for base and head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta. Write the evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/lane-and-model-routing/flight-schema-declares-lanes.html.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
